infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Injected repo vs manager.getRepository inside dataSource.transaction
  desc Same callback, opposite outcome — the binding decides atomicity, not the lexical position.
  compares
    - label Injected repo (this.accountRepo)
      children
        - label Bound to the default manager
          desc Each call runs on its own auto-committed connection
        - label Each write commits alone
          desc The debit is permanent before the next line runs
        - label Not atomic across writes
          desc No single transaction spans the pair
        - label Silent partial commit
          desc A mid-op throw debits without crediting; rollback is a no-op
    - label manager.getRepository(Account)
      children
        - label Bound to the transaction's manager
          desc The shared manager dataSource.transaction yields
        - label Commits only when the callback resolves
          desc Nothing is durable until both writes succeed
        - label Atomic across all writes
          desc Multiple repos, one manager = one unit of work
        - label A throw rolls every write back
          desc The debit is undone with the failed credit
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
